<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RUGBY UNION-BRITISH LIONS BEAT NORTHERN FREE STATE 67-39.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-BRITISH LIONS BEAT NORTHERN FREE STATE 67-39.</headline>
<dateline>WELKOM, South Africa 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British Lions</p>
<p>beat Northern Free State 67-39 (halftime 43-12) in their rugby</p>
<p>tour match on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>British Lions - Tries: Tony Underwood (3), Simon Shaw (2),</p>
<p>Tim Stimpson (2), Kyran Bracken, Neil Back, Mark Regan.</p>
<p>Conversions: Tim Stimpson (7). Penalty: Stimpson.</p>
<p>Northern Free State - Tries: Michael Ehrentraut, Otto</p>
<p>Wagener, Albertus van Buuren, Eric Herbert, penalty try.</p>
<p>Conversions: Eric Herbert (4). Penalties: Herbert (2)</p>
</text>
